{"id": "EUVD-2026-105093", "enisaUuid": "fe9dd325-de2e-3c45-b100-8f0985b8cf3f", "description": "Froxlor from 0.10.0 before 2.3.15 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the SubDomains.delete API command that allows authenticated customers to delete reseller-provisioned main domains by supplying a main domain id. Attackers can bypass the web UI restriction to remove domains, orphan vhost, DNS and subdomain records, and drive subdomains_used below zero to gain extra subdomain allowance.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T15:40:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T18:10:52", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/froxlor/froxlor/security/advisories/GHSA-pp2f-frcg-w8rv", "https://github.com/froxlor/froxlor/commit/078e3f4ba0429390b27baae6aa1cc5d8c9a80010", "https://github.com/froxlor/froxlor/releases/tag/2.3.15", "https://github.com/froxlor/froxlor/blob/2.3.14/lib/Froxlor/Api/Commands/SubDomains.php#L1161-L1211", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/froxlor-0.10.0-before-2.3.15-missing-authorization-via-subdomains-delete-api"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9rxg-hj9r-x482", "CVE-2026-113677"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3dcec1bc-de06-3f4b-bb18-43e78ad7df23", "product": {"name": "Froxlor", "vendor": {"name": "froxlor"}}, "product_version": "0.10.0 <2.3.15"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5d63a51b-7048-3d7e-a6c6-fe5c62d60746", "vendor": {"name": "froxlor"}}], "isExploited": false}